  "summary": "BlackMatter is a ransomware family considered a successor to DarkSide and REvil, targeting both Windows and Linux systems. It uses a Salsa20/RSA-1024 encryption scheme, obfuscates API calls via hashing, and stores its configuration in a custom-named resource section. The malware terminates specific processes and services before encryption and exfiltrates system data to hardcoded C2 servers.",
